      "id": "2m0ktbh",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "1. List of Fundamental Rights"
    },
    {
      "type": "keyFacts",
      "title": "Key Takeaways",
      "items": [
        "Fundamental Rights are enshrined in Part III of the Constitution, covering Articles 12 through 35.",
        "The Right to Equality (Articles 14–18) guarantees equal treatment before the law and prohibits discrimination on grounds of religion, race, caste, sex, or place of birth.",
        "The Right to Freedom (Articles 19–22) protects key liberties including freedom of speech, assembly, and protection in respect of conviction for offences.",
        "Articles 23–24 prohibit human trafficking, forced labor, and child employment in hazardous industries.",
        "Articles 25–28 guarantee freedom of conscience and religious management, while Articles 29–30 protect minority cultural and educational interests.",
        "Article 32 provides the Right to Constitutional Remedies, empowering citizens to move the Supreme Court for the enforcement of Fundamental Rights."
      ],
      "id": "372ibx6"
    },
